A||||10||Dave Gunsul||4.9 questions||||1||
Z||000000||Dave Gunsul||11-24-2001||11:45 AM||||With all this talk of 4.9 caddy swaps I was wondering if anyone could tell me whether this engine is reliable?<BR>I had heard that it wasn't but I don't have any real knowledge of this engine so if this is incorrect I would like to know.<BR>Obviously any V8 in a Fiero is going to be fairly quick so i'm not really asking anything about the performance issue i just want to know how this engine lasts or if there's any problems with it breaking down?<BR>Any info that anyone has would be greatly appreciated. <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000001||Daleford||11-24-2001||11:52 AM||||Dave.  Just installed one with 100 thousand miles on it, and it runs like a new engine. Installed complete Caddy drivetrain in a Kitcar [Fiero] chassis and didn't even separate engine, trans, or cradle.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||11-24-2001||12:10 PM||||Does the ENTIRE Caddy cradle fit(bolt up) directly to our Fiero's??? <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/texas_1.gif">          <BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Daleford||11-24-2001||12:17 PM||||Not really.  The two rear horns of the cradle get cut off and boxed.  A new crossmember has to be built to pick up what's left.  In the front the horns get cut back and a new extension attached that runs forward to the Fiero horizontal bolt cradle mount. Keep in mind, this is on a 7 inch stretch chassis.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||11-24-2001||03:50 PM||||I think Ed Parks used the term "bulletproof".<BR>Apparently, Caddys with this engine are seen frequently at auctions, with 200,000 miles. Still running fine. <BR>The early predecessor to the 4.5 and 4.9 was the 4100. It was a real POS, but the bugs have been worked out in the later engines, especially the PFI ones.<BR>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||11-24-2001||04:37 PM||||Kind like what first happened to Fiero's reputation.<BR>4.1's caddy learned, 4.5 greatly improved and 4.9 excellent so GM drops it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||11-24-2001||11:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PBJ:<BR><B>Kind like what first happened to Fiero's reputation.<BR>4.1's caddy learned, 4.5 greatly improved and 4.9 excellent so GM drops it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They may have dropped it, but at least they replaced it with the Northstar.<BR>GM has a way of eating its young, however...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||11-25-2001||03:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><BR>The early predecessor to the 4.5 and 4.9 was the 4100. It was a real POS, but the bugs have been worked out in the later engines, especially the PFI ones.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ah ha, this is where my confusion must be coming from. I must've heard the bad about the 4.1 and gotten it confused.<BR>Looks like I owe a couple-a people an apology<BR>now. Thanks for all the replies and helping me to get this issue straight!<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000008||kevin||11-26-2001||03:49 PM||||How much extra weight does the 4.9 add to the Fiero? SOunds like a great swap. Anyone know the weight issues? I would hate to gain power at the expense of precise handling.||||reg||1
Z||000009||rockcrawl||11-26-2001||04:02 PM||||2.5 liter Tech4- 302.3 lb.<BR>2.8 liter V6- 345-376 lb. depending on source. Cadillac 4.5/4.9 liter PFI V8- 371 lb. with all accesories including A/C, ready to be installed in a Fiero.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/weights.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/weights.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||11-26-2001||05:18 PM||||can you throw the weight of a 3.4tdc in there too if someone has it?||||reg||1
